d" class=3D"">set bits</button></span> in its binary representation (also k=
nown as the <a href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_weight" target=
=3D"_blank">Hamming weight</a>).</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<div class=3D"example-block">
<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=3D"example-io">n =3D 11</span></p>

<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=3D"example-io">3</span></p>

<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>

<p>The input binary string <strong>1011</strong> has a total of three set b=
its.</p>
</div>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<div class=3D"example-block">
<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=3D"example-io">n =3D 128</span></p>

<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=3D"example-io">1</span></p>

<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>

<p>The input binary string <strong>10000000</strong> has a total of one set=
 bit.</p>
</div>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 3:</strong></p>

<div class=3D"example-block">
<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=3D"example-io">n =3D 2147483645</spa=
n></p>

<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=3D"example-io">30</span></p>

<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>

<p>The input binary string <strong>1111111111111111111111111111101</strong>=
 has a total of thirty set bits.</p>
</div>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D n &lt;=3D 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li>
</ul>

